# Contributor: unex <7575866+unex@users.noreply.github.com>
# Maintainer: unex <7575866+unex@users.noreply.github.com>
# Board layer of the uc-pxx panels (UC-P10, UC-P8): the board file board.sh
# (with the update hooks tsx_board_pre_update and tsx_board_post_update), the
# hardware tools and services, the audio configuration, the key map and the
# switch tool rtl8363-init. It is the part of rootfs/overlay of uc-pxx-linux
# that the board owns. Other owners of overlay files:
#   uc-pxx-boot-tools   the boot control (the four pinned scripts), uc-pxx-reboot
#                       and uc-pxx-post-update
#   tsx-keys            etc/apk/keys
#   the image build     etc/fstab and etc/inittab (profiles/image.list)
# package() stops when the overlay has a file that no list below names, so a
# new board file cannot go missing without a note.
#
# board.sh needs tsx-linux-common 0.3.12: TSX_PKG_PREFIX and the board hooks of
# tsx-autoupdate. An older tsx-autoupdate would upgrade system_a without
# uc-pxx-arm-slot, so the floor is a depends of this package.
# tsx_board_post_update writes the kernel of uc-pxx-kernel-lts into boot_a
# after a tsx-autoupdate install (uc-pxx-update-boot write). Only tsx-autoupdate
# 0.3.12 or newer runs that hook with the run lock and the restart block. The
# upgrade that brings it runs the old tsx-autoupdate, which writes no kernel:
# install it before a kernel update. The hook only runs
# /usr/sbin/uc-pxx-post-update of uc-pxx-boot-tools, so uc-pxx-boot-tools
# 0.1.0-r2 is the floor.
# 0.1.0-r2: the first public build (r1 was a private build).
# 0.2.0-r0: the both-slot release (uc-pxx-linux mainline-linux-int). The
# service uc-pxx-lvm mounts /data itself (the line "# uc-pxx-data-mount: 1"):
# the partition named userdata when it is ext4 tsxdata, else the phase-1 LVM
# volume; the image fstab has no /data line. uc-pxx-firmware reads
# /data/uc-pxx/firmware first. New: uc-pxx-data-migrate and
# uc-pxx-data-release (the userdata tools of step 2 of the mainline install;
# pinned in _pins, not yet in the safety rules). It needs the both-slot boot
# control (uc-pxx-boot-tools 0.2.0) and the both-slot initramfs (the
# uc-pxx-kernel-lts of the same release): /data, the root of the booted slot
# and the slot guard of the updaters belong together (MAINLINE-LINUX-INT §7).
# 2026-11-12: the 0.2.0 pins are in the UC-P10 safety rules (owner approval 2026-11-11)
# (uc-pxx/RULES-PINS); the source is the tag board-v0.2.0 (uc-pxx-linux 26c95ca).
#
# Sources:
#  - the GitHub archive of the tag board-v$pkgver of uc-pxx-linux
#  - uc-pxx-tools-bundle.tar.zst of the tsx-aports release _tbundle_tag
#    (rtl8363-init, built with the GPL Realtek switch SDK, see
#    tools/rtl8363-init of uc-pxx-linux)
# The sums at the end are all zeros until the tag board-v0.2.0 and the
# release uc-pxx-tools-20261110 exist (a local build uses a snapshot and
# the staged bundle, README.md "uc-pxx packages").
SRCDEST="$startdir/dist"
pkgname=uc-pxx-board
pkgver=0.2.0
pkgrel=0
_tbundle_tag=uc-pxx-tools-20261110
pkgdesc="uc-pxx board layer: board file, hardware tools, services, audio and the switch tool"
url="https://github.com/tsx-mainline/uc-pxx-linux"
arch="aarch64"
license="GPL-2.0-or-later"
# e2fsprogs: mkfs.ext4 and e2fsck of uc-pxx-data-migrate; util-linux-misc:
# blkdiscard. The kernel floor is the first kernel package with the
# both-slot initramfs.
depends="alsa-utils e2fsprogs evtest iw lvm2 python3 tsx-autoupdate>=0.3.12 tsx-base>=0.3.12 uc-pxx-boot-tools>=0.2.0-r0
	uc-pxx-kernel-lts>=6.18.54_git20261110-r0 util-linux-misc wireless-regdb"
# /etc/securetty replaces the one of busybox (and of tsx-base up to 0.2.1).
replaces="busybox tsx-base"
# The panel software lives in /usr/local, as in the image. !strip keeps the
# bytes of the tested rtl8363-init.
options="!fhs !strip"
source="uc-pxx-linux-$pkgver.tar.gz::https://github.com/tsx-mainline/uc-pxx-linux/archive/refs/tags/board-v$pkgver.tar.gz
	https://github.com/tsx-mainline/tsx-aports/releases/download/$_tbundle_tag/uc-pxx-tools-bundle.tar.zst
	"
builddir="$srcdir/uc-pxx-linux-board-v$pkgver"

# The files of rootfs/overlay that this package owns.
_files="
